  "term": "lateral corticospinal tract",
  "definition": "In this biological context, the lateral corticospinal tract is the motor pathway described as carrying monosynaptic connections from the motor cortex to distal muscles. The article contrasts it with the ventromedial corticospinal tract, which it links to primarily polysynaptic innervation of proximal muscles.",
